Writer undo uses the current view only when it shows the same document

Under LibreOfficeKit, sw::UndoManager::impl_DoUndoRedo takes its edit
shell from SfxViewShell::Current(). While a second document loads it
has no view yet, so the current view belongs to the first document.
The DOCX import undoes a paragraph whose style it cannot apply (a
pStyle with no definition), and that undo moved the first document's
cursor to node indices of the second: with two such paragraphs the
index runs past the first document's nodes and the worker dies with
an access violation, which the crash handler ends with exit code 0
(Ely R15.13c). The current view now counts only for its own document;
otherwise the document's own edit shell is used, as without LOK.
diff --git a/sw/source/core/undo/docundo.cxx b/sw/source/core/undo/docundo.cxx
index 8f9fc0e4e..5f68fb5ca 100644
--- a/sw/source/core/undo/docundo.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/core/undo/docundo.cxx
@@ -673,6 +673,9 @@ bool UndoManager::impl_DoUndoRedo(UndoOrRedoType undoOrRedo, size_t nUndoOffset)
     UnoActionContext c(& rDoc); // exception-safe StartAllAction/EndAllAction
 
     SwView* pViewShell = dynamic_cast<SwView*>(SfxViewShell::Current());
+    // The current view may show another document.
+    if (pViewShell && pViewShell->GetDocShell()->GetDoc() != &rDoc)
+        pViewShell = nullptr;
     SwEditShell *const pEditShell(
         comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive() && pViewShell ? pViewShell->GetWrtShellPtr()
         : rDoc.GetEditShell());
